{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev","id":302239,"title":"Get the Lead Out: Complex Refinements (Open Dev)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-04T08:52:30-08:00","id":302239,"title":"Get the Lead Out: Complex Refinements (Open Dev)","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/its-complicated/\" target=\"_blank\">Basic Refinements are next week.</a><br /> <br /> So apparently glamourweaver called it: Mercurius is a complex refinement and process of elimination indicates that Lead is a basic one. Seems as sensible a switch as any, though it seems we have a doubling up of affinity Transmutations going from the 1e lists. (Then again, Disquietism and Vulcanus seem like the most suitable ones to duplicate for basic and complex, respectively, so that salves the niggling attack of geek-OCD somewhat.)<br /> <br /> Also, the River of Death continues to be a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-04-2014, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T10:13:52-08:00","id":302421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev#post302239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the River of Death continues to be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is River of Death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-04-2014, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T10:25:08-08:00","id":302431,"title":"","content":"Nice. Good overview, and I think it actually summed up some of the Refinements like Cobalus better (at least for me) than the books did.<br /> <br /> The Phosphorus write-up also made me suddenly antsy to find a Promethean game and try out my escape artist Tammuz character concept; was originally thinking he'd start with Ferrum before jumping to Cuprum, but now I'm thinking Phosphorum might be a good fit somewhere in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T10:28:42-08:00","id":302436,"title":"","content":"i think its the River from the opening fiction from Pandoras Book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T12:12:26-08:00","id":302522,"title":"","content":"It's also what Prometheans are described experiencing in their visits to the Underworld in &quot;Book of the Dead&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> So the biggest surprise here is that Mercurius is a Complex Refinement, which means Plumbum is Basic. This certainly makes thematic sense! Plumbum should be a valid starting position - a Promethean struggling with the &quot;What am I?&quot; question. The higher mysteries of Pyros are more esoteric by definition.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering though what it means for the Transmutation line up. Will Quicksilver and Phosphorus both favor Vulcanus? Will Tin and Lead both favor Disquietism?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T12:57:22-08:00","id":302558,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:monospace\">I'm still waiting for the asbestos refinement</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:18:11-08:00","id":302573,"title":"","content":"Not much changed from 1ed except maybe Cobalus absorbing the previous Centimani &quot;good side&quot; of the Pilgrimage, experiencing human evil and such, and Argentum with a bigger focus on studying the supernatural rather than mimicking it. I was expecting to see more about the Roles, guess we have to wait to individual Refinements write-ups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T14:35:34-08:00","id":302697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=302573#post302573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not much changed from 1ed except maybe Cobalus absorbing the previous Centimani &quot;good side&quot; of the Pilgrimage, experiencing human evil and such, and Argentum with a bigger focus on studying the supernatural rather than mimicking it. I was expecting to see more about the Roles, guess we have to wait to individual Refinements write-ups.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really liking the re-focused take on Argentum. As my favourite refinement I'm glad to see it moving away from just a basic mimicry philosophy. <br /> <br /> I think Cobalus is massively improved by the injection of the &quot;good side&quot; of the Centimantani philosophy about studying human evil. Aes likewise seems to a have a better write up and focus now then it did in 1E. <br /> <br /> I'm kinda sorry to see one of the &quot;legitimizing&quot; elements of the Centimantani get cut out of them. They were, for me the most well written group of antagonists in any game line in 1st Edition NWoD (ahead of even groups like The Brood and the Seers for my money, despite both of these groups getting (for my money) the best faction books of their respective lines). They came across in Pandora's book as <i>almost</i> a completely legitimate alternative philosophy to the more traditional refinements. <br /> <br /> While I don't mind their more villianious aspects getting toned up in 2E Promethean, I do hope some of the obvious TLC they received from the original write up remains. Making them kinda understandable and a little bit tragic goes a long way I feel. Rather then framing them as body-horror driven serial killer enthusiasts. Still I'm holding off any further ideas about them as a &quot;not-refinement&quot; until they get a weekly preview (hopefully in a couple of weeks).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T19:59:03-08:00","id":302915,"title":"","content":"Matt confirmed that yes Vulcanus appears twice with the Complex Refinements (and thus isn't favored by any of the Basic ones), and the reverse is true of Disquietism. I suppose the thematic associations are way more important than symmetry in that regard. As it stands every Refinement favors one Transmutation type that they alone favor. For Phosphorum that's &quot;Luciferus&quot;, about which your guess is as good as mine. Perhaps something to aid in resurrection (in a way other than the Revivification Bestowment) and following other Prometheans to the River of Death?<br /> <br /> Assuming the Refinements all still have a one word focus (Aurum = Mortality, Mercurius = Pyros, Cuprum = Self, Stannum = Torment, Cobalus = Impurity; etc etc) I really wonder what Phosphorum's is.. Life? Death?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T21:11:53-08:00","id":302950,"title":"","content":"Defiance, I think. In that they defy risk, danger and death on their path for life and experience. Make any sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T21:20:54-08:00","id":302956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wild-Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=302950#post302950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Defiance, I think. In that they defy risk, danger and death on their path for life and experience. Make any sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't defy risk and death - they embrace it. They idea of someone who is &quot;death-defying&quot; is that they're so skilled they can survive taking incredible risks; but the point of the Light-Bringers isn't that they make the leap over the 30 flaming school buses (that's more of a Titan/Ferrum theme), it's that they're perfectly happy to fail and crash into them while laughing &quot;YOLO!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-05-2014, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T22:00:08-08:00","id":302981,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I wonder if the authors thought of Alchemists as a field of study for Mystics.<br /> <br /> That might be a bit too much like the old centimanni though for some though, but I think studying humanity through the lens of those who sell it piece by piece through equivalent exchange for their goals would be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T22:29:00-08:00","id":302999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=302981#post302981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmm, I wonder if the authors thought of Alchemists as a field of study for Mystics.<br /> <br /> That might be a bit too much like the old centimanni though for some though, but I think studying humanity through the lens of those who sell it piece by piece through equivalent exchange for their goals would be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Generally I'd rule at my own table that things that fall under the Divine Fire/Alchemy metaphysics unique to PtC don't qualify for an Argentum focus. Chasing down info on Qashmallim for example would generally be a Mercurius thing (unless it's a specific focus on the Lilithim - then it's a direct path to becoming Centimani).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T22:46:22-08:00","id":303004,"title":"","content":"Plumbum becoming core is something I've wanted for /years/! And it's great to see the Cobalus get some more wordcount; I can't wait for the fiction on Gold-Cobalt movement, in either direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T01:04:32-08:00","id":303091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=302999#post302999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Generally I'd rule at my own table that things that fall under the Divine Fire/Alchemy metaphysics unique to PtC don't qualify for an Argentum focus. Chasing down info on Qashmallim for example would generally be a Mercurius thing (unless it's a specific focus on the Lilithim - then it's a direct path to becoming Centimani).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done this as well in the past (well, in the game notes, having never found a group willing to give Promethean more then a glance). <br /> <br /> In general I would say that Qashmallim fall under &quot;study of Pyros/Azoth&quot; that is part of Mercurius. Pandorans and Lilithim are very much part of the focus of Centimani. <br /> <br /> Alchemists...not sure. Until I see the full write up for them I honestly can't say. At the moment I'm leaning on them being more of a Mercurius thing again, because well...alchemy and an obsession with vitriol. <br /> <br /> Even if you discount all the above sources and only use the GMC core there is still plenty for Argentum followers to look into, to name a few:<br /> Ghosts, Spirits, Angels and &quot;weird&quot; mortals (people with the supernatural merits detailed in GMC). <br /> <br /> Considering that Hurt Locker is going to have a couple more of those &quot;weird&quot; mortal merits as well, there is plenty for you to use in the core line alone. <br /> <br /> Stuff from other games lines that can be added to that and fits Promethean well without necessarily involving other PC templates is also possible. <br /> <br /> Underworld stuff fits with the River of Death thing. Meaning Avernian gates and the Rivers of the Underworld along with entities like Cthonians, Psychopomps and Korboroi.<br /> <br /> General Shadow stuff (thanks to the Ulgan), so verges, wounds, glades and null areas with Spirits obviously as the main entity of focus, though Urged, Ridden and Claimed work as well, as well as hosts and Idigam if you want to go there. <br /> <br /> Mummy works well in general as a good contrast to Promethean but has a lot of similarities as the same time with relics, vestiges, odd &quot;neverborn&quot; like entities, chimerical monsters, Shuanksen and Sadikh. <br /> <br /> Demon of couse adds the GM as a contrast to the Principle and adds Stigmatics, Cryptids/Cryptoflora, Clockwork beings and Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd avoid adding Vampire, Mage or Changeling stuff but that's just personal taste in regards to Prometheans themes interacting with those of these others games. I'd also avoid adding PC templates whole sale save maybe Mummy's and Demons, once again though thats just a case of personal choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T06:19:04-08:00","id":303228,"title":"","content":"I've actually thought for a while that a Promethean meeting a mage of the Uncrowned Kings legacy (or at least becoming pen pals, of a sort) could inspire one to take up Argentum. Or Mercurius. Or move from one to the other. The point is the legacy's ideal of alchemy as inner change/betterment through external effort resonates pretty strongly with Promethean's themes and the goal of the Pilgrimage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T08:20:08-08:00","id":303317,"title":"","content":"Super happy to see a non-binary character in the write up. Hope it stays for the full book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3707-thediabadass","name":"TheDiabadass","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T10:13:02-08:00","id":303380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheDiabadass</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=303317#post303317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Super happy to see a non-binary character in the write up. Hope it stays for the full book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm curious whether they are also intersex, as it would make sense for a (Mercurius) Promethean or a Demiurge to make their creation &quot;The Rebis&quot; (sacred alchemical 'hermaphrodite').","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T13:11:31-08:00","id":303665,"title":"","content":"When Argentum was first published, the only other WoD gamelines that existed were Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage. I look forward to seeing the new take on said Refinement now that we have nine gamelines and counting \u2014 especially with the post-GMC \u201cdifferent kinds of ephemera\u201d rule, which is designed to more or less isolate the various gamelines\u2019 ephemeral beings from each other, and implies that the various \u201cghosts and spirits\u201d Spiritus Transmutations ought to be recast as \u201cghosts <i>or</i> spirits\u201d (<i>or</i> angels, <i>or</i> Strix, <i>or</i> Supernal Beings, etc.)<br /> <br /> And bear in mind that there\u2019s more to the supernatural denizens of the World of Darkness than just \u201ctemplates and ephemera\u201d. <b>Promethean</b>\u2019s own Pandorans were arguably the first nWoD monsters to be published that were neither template noe ephemeral; but they\u2019ve been followed up by <b>Changeling</b>\u2019s hobgoblins and Gentry and <b>Demon</b>\u2019s cryptids; and who knows <i>what</i> <b>Beast</b> is going to bring to the table? <br /> <br /> And then there are the Outsiders from <b>Glimpses of the Unknown</b> (who I\u2019m hoping will be featured in the second edition of the WoD core). If nothing else, a follower of Argentum who deals with Outsiders would give you a way of using the Refinement without doing crossovers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-08-2014, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T18:56:56-08:00","id":303991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=303380#post303380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm curious whether they are also intersex, as it would make sense for a (Mercurius) Promethean or a Demiurge to make their creation &quot;The Rebis&quot; (sacred alchemical 'hermaphrodite').</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be honest, I would prefer it if they had two separate characters, one agender (or non-binary of any sort) and one intersex more than if they made them the same character. I understand that intersex can identify outside of the binary, but I think it would help dispel the idea that they have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3707-thediabadass","name":"TheDiabadass","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T20:18:20-08:00","id":304076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheDiabadass</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=303991#post303991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To be honest, I would prefer it if they had two separate characters, one agender (or non-binary of any sort) and one intersex more than if they made them the same character. I understand that intersex can identify outside of the binary, but I think it would help dispel the idea that they have to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough. I just mention it because I had a Promethean character who was intentionally created by a Mercurius predecessor as an Alchemical Rebis from male and female body-parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T23:36:25-08:00","id":304226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=302999#post302999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Generally I'd rule at my own table that things that fall under the Divine Fire/Alchemy metaphysics unique to PtC don't qualify for an Argentum focus. Chasing down info on Qashmallim for example would generally be a Mercurius thing (unless it's a specific focus on the Lilithim - then it's a direct path to becoming Centimani).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless they've seriously changed the focus (learning about humanity by studying the monsters they can turn into) the other Pyros related things don't qualify for mystics: neither pandorans nor quashmallam were ever human, and well clones are shoddy imitations so I don't see them being a very rewarding study. <br /> <br /> <br /> Plus, I typed that they would study alchemists, not alchemy. Not that say a mystic trying to expand their knowledge of alchemy by studying cruac is wrong hurting fun, but the mystics as a whole are far more Jane Goodall than Tesla, unless, again, that they really changed focus in sec ed. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T09:06:47-08:00","id":304656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheDiabadass</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=303317#post303317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Super happy to see a non-binary character in the write up. Hope it stays for the full book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alex is, in fact, staying for the book - that particular character was written by new OPP author Vera Vartanian, and isn't the only instance of non-binary (and non-cis, for that matter) characters in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T09:31:58-08:00","id":304676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=304656#post304656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alex is, in fact, staying for the book - that particular character was written by new OPP author Vera Vartanian, and isn't the only instance of non-binary (and non-cis, for that matter) characters in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have I ever told you how cool OPP is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:12:40-08:00","id":304865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=304676#post304676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have I ever told you how cool OPP is?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We do our best. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Honestly, though, I had a wake-up call a year or so ago. I was talking to a longtime WW player, and she mentioned that early WW games (like, VtM 1st Ed) were some of the few that ever bothered using female pronouns, and thus made her feel like she was allowed to play. And I though, wow, I had never considered that, partially because my groups have always been pretty well mixed, but also because duh, I'm a dude. Of <i>course</i> I'm allowed. <br /> <br /> So, when I'm developing games for OPP (and for my own company), I try make it clear: Everyone's welcome. These games are awesome, you get to play awesome characters, you should be able to see something you recognize in those characters. And, for me as a writer, that means if I don't know how to write certain kinds of characters, I need to a) learn or b) hire someone who does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T13:32:35-08:00","id":304950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=304865#post304865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We do our best.</div> </div> </div> </div>You all do VERY well with those things, sir.<br /> <br /> My troupe consists of exactly ONE cis-male gamer, and the rest of us are either 'nonbinary' or otherwise of the lady-persuasion. ALL of us have experience with the transformative experiences that <b>Promethean: the Created</b> touches upon, too. It's not WHY we play the game, nor is it what ever session is about. That said, no one at my table feels excluded for who she is, and I cannot imagine a game where anyone would do. That fact is based on my experience alone, of course, but much of my gaming experience is from the World(s) of Darkness games.<br /> <br /> *shrug*<br /> <br /> ...That's just my 2p worth, but know that my buy-in for the game is richer for it. Thanks for keeping up that excellent level of work, <b>blackhatmatt</b>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T18:00:07-08:00","id":305141,"title":"","content":"Ideas for additional (pejorative) nicknames...<br /> <br /> Aes: Sentries, <b>Dogs</b><br /> Argentum: Mystics; <b>Thralls</b><br /> Cobalus: Cathars;<b> Unclean</b><br /> Mercurius: Savants; <b>Serpents</b><br /> Phosphorum: Light-Bringers; <b>Moths</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T20:33:52-08:00","id":305244,"title":"","content":"I dunno, I like &quot;Kobolds&quot; for Cobalus. Or Knockers.<br /> <br /> Phosphorum could be Phoenixes, or Mayflies...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T21:38:12-08:00","id":305294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=305244#post305244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, I like &quot;Kobolds&quot; for Cobalus. Or Knockers.<br /> <br /> Phosphorum could be Phoenixes, or Mayflies...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kobolds works given the etymology.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.donmarquis.org/themoth.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Moths comes specifically from one of the inspiration sources for the Light-Bringers that Matt shared.</a> Given the idea that moths will burn themselves alive, it fits better than the merely short lived (Mayflies), or the not at all pejorative (Phoenixes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T20:31:11-08:00","id":307821,"title":"","content":"Matt, I don't suppose you can share anything about the Luciferus Transmutations yet? I'm just hoping they aren't literal luminescence and immolation, as that would majorly take the wind out of the historic Lineage I'm working on as a potential submission (and failing that, fan project).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T21:24:07-08:00","id":307891,"title":"","content":"Immolation ought not venture far from Vulcanus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T10:19:09-08:00","id":308325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=307821#post307821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matt, I don't suppose you can share anything about the Luciferus Transmutations yet? I'm just hoping they aren't literal luminescence and immolation, as that would majorly take the wind out of the historic Lineage I'm working on as a potential submission (and failing that, fan project).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They're not <i>all</i> that, but that's some of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T12:49:54-08:00","id":309393,"title":"","content":"I'll echo the sentiment that it's awesome to see a character that's outside of the gender binary. What's more, Promethean is a wonderful place to explore those sorts of issues. Gender is another kind of construct, after all. <hr /><br /> Basic refinement writeups are up, FYI! <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/first-principles-basic-refinements/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/first-princip...c-refinements/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","user":"Metamurpho","date":". 11-11-2014, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T14:01:56-08:00","id":310552,"title":"","content":"Just a note here, from an amateur Latin scholar: &quot;Luciferus&quot; isn't a word. It should be just &quot;Lucifer&quot; (if masculine) or &quot;Luciferum&quot; (if neuter.) Admittedly, Latin has not traditionally been WW/OP's strong suit, but this one just bugs me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T05:38:49-08:00","id":311140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=310552#post310552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a note here, from an amateur Latin scholar: &quot;Luciferus&quot; isn't a word. It should be just &quot;Lucifer&quot; (if masculine) or &quot;Luciferum&quot; (if neuter.) Admittedly, Latin has not traditionally been WW/OP's strong suit, but this one just bugs me.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we started using correct Latin now, people would think we'd been replaced by pod people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T11:25:28-08:00","id":313120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=304865#post304865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly, though, I had a wake-up call a year or so ago. I was talking to a longtime WW player, and she mentioned that early WW games (like, VtM 1st Ed) were some of the few that ever bothered using female pronouns, and thus made her feel like she was allowed to play. And I though, wow, I had never considered that, partially because my groups have always been pretty well mixed, but also because duh, I'm a dude. Of <i>course</i> I'm allowed.<br /> <br /> So, when I'm developing games for OPP (and for my own company), I try make it clear: Everyone's welcome. These games are awesome, you get to play awesome characters, you should be able to see something you recognize in those characters. And, for me as a writer, that means if I don't know how to write certain kinds of characters, I need to a) learn or b) hire someone who does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Im currently on the vampire boards as thats what I'm running, but after Promethean 2E comes out, I think I just have to buy it now. haha. Honestly though, knowing that you guys are putting in this kind of effort brings a tear to my eye. It may not seem like much to cis-gamers, but it means a lot to little old non-binary me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3707-thediabadass","name":"TheDiabadass","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T15:33:53-08:00","id":314858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/302239-get-the-lead-out-complex-refinements-open-dev?p=311140#post311140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we started using correct Latin now, people would think we'd been replaced by pod people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, considering the quantity and quality of the material from Onyx Path, I already believe that you lot have been 'pod people' for years now! The questionable Latin is just a ruse to keep us from knowing who and what you really are, no doubt.<br /> <br /> ...And I actually KNOW some human beings. Really. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}